# moz-official -- DESKTOP half (LW-M1-04).
#
# Split out of patches/moz-official.patch, a straddler. The two core GMP hunks
# (dom/media/gmp/ChromiumCDMAdapter.cpp, media/gmp-clearkey/0.1/gmp-clearkey.cpp)
# are in patches/moz-official-common.patch; common + desktop together are, byte
# for byte, the hunks of the original patch, in the original order within each
# half.
#
# What is here (re-derived for Firefox 157 from upstream LibreWolf's
# regenerated patches/moz-official.patch, the browser/ hunks taken verbatim):
#   browser/base/content/browser-development-helpers.js
#                                         DevelopmentHelpers.init() only binds
#                                         quickRestart and adds the shortcut when
#                                         Services.prefs.getBoolPref(
#                                           "librewolf.devHelpers", false)
#   browser/base/content/browser-main.js  drops the !AppConstants.MOZILLA_OFFICIAL
#                                         guard: browser-development-helpers.js
#                                         is always loaded (the pref gate is
#                                         now inside init(), above)
#   browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest
#                                         drops #ifndef MOZILLA_OFFICIAL /
#                                         #endif around the
#                                         browser-window-delayed-startup category
#                                         entry that calls DevelopmentHelpers.init
#   browser/base/jar.mn                   drops the #ifndef MOZILLA_OFFICIAL /
#                                         #endif around the packaging line for
#                                         browser-development-helpers.js
#
# History: up to Firefox 153 the init call was a hard-coded
# `if (!AppConstants.MOZILLA_OFFICIAL) DevelopmentHelpers.init()` in
# browser/base/content/browser-init.js, and this patch rewrote that test (and the
# matching one in browser-main.js) to the pref. Firefox moved the call into a
# BrowserComponents.manifest delayed-startup category, so the pref check moved
# into init() itself. The behaviour is unchanged: helper off unless the pref is
# true. References below to "the browser-init hunk" mean this init hook in either
# shape.
#
# Together these keep the upstream "local development" helper -- the
# accel+alt+R quick-restart command, key and File-menu item defined in
# browser/base/content/browser-development-helpers.js -- available in an
# official LibreWolf build, behind librewolf.devHelpers, which
# settings/librewolf.cfg:756 defaults to false.
#
# Why it is desktop-only: all four files are under browser/.
# browser/app.mozbuild:11 (`DIRS += ["/browser"]`) is what pulls /browser into a
# build and mobile/android/app.mozbuild never does, so these files are not in an
# Android build at all and the hunks could not apply to one.
#
# ==========================================================================
# DOES mobile/android HAVE AN EQUIVALENT OF THE browser-init HUNK?  NO.
# ==========================================================================
# Asked and answered against the pristine firefox-153.0.4 tree, so the next
# reader does not have to re-derive it. There is no Android counterpart, none is
# needed, and there is deliberately no patches/android/moz-official-android.patch;
# assets/patches/android.txt records the same conclusion.
#
# The evidence:
#
#   1. DevelopmentHelpers exists nowhere else. `grep -rl "DevelopmentHelpers\|
#      development-helpers"` over the whole 153 tree returned exactly six files: the
#      three patched here, browser/base/content/browser-development-helpers.js
#      itself, and two devtools files that only name it in a comment while
#      reimplementing it --
#      devtools/server/actors/descriptors/process.js:228 ("This aims at
#      replicate `DevelopmentHelpers.quickRestart`", inside reloadDescriptor,
#      which does the same startupcache-invalidate + MOZ_DISABLE_SAFE_MODE_KEY +
#      eAttemptQuit|eRestart sequence) and
#      devtools/client/webconsole/webconsole-ui.js:713 ("This is the same as
#      DevelopmentHelpers.quickRestart, but it runs in all builds (even
#      official)"). Neither is MOZILLA_OFFICIAL-gated, so neither needs this
#      patch -- and devtools/server ships on Android unguarded
#      (devtools/moz.build:11-16), so the one of the two that is common already
#      carries the behaviour there. Nothing under mobile/ mentions the helper.
#
#   2. The helper is XUL-only by construction. addRestartShortcut() calls
#      document.createXULElement("command"/"key"/"menuitem") and appends to
#      #mainCommandSet, #mainKeyset and #menu_FilePopup -- the desktop browser
#      window's XUL. GeckoView has no such document, so even a hypothetical
#      Android port of the file would have nothing to attach to.
#
#   3. Android's MOZILLA_OFFICIAL uses are all a different shape. Every hit of
#      `grep -rn MOZILLA_OFFICIAL mobile/` is one of:
#        * mozconfig exports (mobile/android/config/mozconfigs/**, e.g.
#          android-arm/nightly:8), i.e. build inputs;
#        * Gradle plumbing (mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle:37,243,391-393,
#          mobile/android/geckoview/build.gradle:78,389,
#          gradle/{debug_level,mozconfig,with_gecko_binaries}.gradle,
#          gradle/plugins/.../MachExec.kt), which turns the substitution into
#          BuildConfig.MOZILLA_OFFICIAL and skips tasks;
#        * Java/Kotlin runtime feature gates on that BuildConfig flag: fenix
#          BaseBrowserFragment.kt:1279 (WebAuthnFeature -- "only works on Fenix
#          when built on Mozilla infrastructure"), geckoview
#          WebAuthnTokenManager.java:202,440,601,630, CrashHandler.java:605,
#          GeckoAppShell.java:142, ContentBlocking.java:655 (safebrowsing
#          provider name), and a row of `DEBUG = !BuildConfig.MOZILLA_OFFICIAL`
#          log switches in the media/HLS classes.
#      Not one of them is a chrome-JS `if (!AppConstants.MOZILLA_OFFICIAL)` init
#      hook, and not one gates a developer restart shortcut. No .js, .mjs or
#      jar.mn under mobile/ mentions MOZILLA_OFFICIAL at all.
#
#   4. Those Java/Kotlin gates are the wrong thing to convert anyway. They are
#      compiled against BuildConfig, decided by Gradle before any pref exists,
#      and the change here is specifically "keep a dev convenience that upstream
#      drops in official builds, behind a pref". Android has no such convenience
#      to keep. Flipping MOZILLA_OFFICIAL on Android would instead re-enable
#      debug logging and change the safebrowsing provider -- unrelated, and
#      unwanted, changes.
#
#   So: the browser-init hunk has no Android equivalent, and the common half is
#   the whole of moz-official that reaches Android. If an Android build ever
#   wants a quick-restart affordance it is new work in patches/android/, not a
#   port of this hunk.
#
diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser-development-helpers.js b/browser/base/content/browser-development-helpers.js
index 5155b28..8dea266 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/browser-development-helpers.js
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser-development-helpers.js
@@ -9,8 +9,10 @@
 
 var DevelopmentHelpers = {
   init() {
-    this.quickRestart = this.quickRestart.bind(this);
-    this.addRestartShortcut();
+    if (Services.prefs.getBoolPref("librewolf.devHelpers", false)) {
+      this.quickRestart = this.quickRestart.bind(this);
+      this.addRestartShortcut();
+    }
   },
 
   quickRestart() {
diff --git a/browser/base/content/browser-main.js b/browser/base/content/browser-main.js
index 1ff101a..6b02e5a 100644
--- a/browser/base/content/browser-main.js
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser-main.js
@@ -11,9 +11,7 @@
   if (AppConstants.MOZ_DATA_REPORTING) {
     Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/browser-data-submission-info-bar.js", this);
   }
-  if (!AppConstants.MOZILLA_OFFICIAL) {
-    Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/browser-development-helpers.js", this);
-  }
+  Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/browser-development-helpers.js", this);
   Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/browser-pageActions.js", this);
   Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", this);
   Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript("chrome://browser/content/browser-customtitlebar.js", this);
diff --git a/browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest b/browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest
index 17f4eaf..988d852 100644
--- a/browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest
+++ b/browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest
@@ -86,9 +86,7 @@ category browser-window-delayed-startup chrome://browser/content/browser-fullScr
 #ifdef MOZ_DATA_REPORTING
 category browser-window-delayed-startup chrome://browser/content/browser-data-submission-info-bar.js gDataNotificationInfoBar.init
 #endif
-#ifndef MOZILLA_OFFICIAL
 category browser-window-delayed-startup chrome://browser/content/browser-development-helpers.js DevelopmentHelpers.init
-#endif
 category browser-window-delayed-startup chrome://browser/content/browser-addons.js gExtensionsNotifications.init
 category browser-window-delayed-startup chrome://browser/content/browser-captivePortal.js CaptivePortalWatcher.delayedStartup
 
diff --git a/browser/base/jar.mn b/browser/base/jar.mn
index 22550de..470b23f 100644
--- a/browser/base/jar.mn
+++ b/browser/base/jar.mn
@@ -45,9 +45,7 @@ browser.jar:
         content/browser/browser-context.js            (content/browser-context.js)
         content/browser/browser-customization.js      (content/browser-customization.js)
         content/browser/browser-data-submission-info-bar.js (content/browser-data-submission-info-bar.js)
-#ifndef MOZILLA_OFFICIAL
         content/browser/browser-development-helpers.js (content/browser-development-helpers.js)
-#endif
         content/browser/browser-fullScreenAndPointerLock.js (content/browser-fullScreenAndPointerLock.js)
         content/browser/browser-gestureSupport.js           (content/browser-gestureSupport.js)
         content/browser/browser-init.js                     (content/browser-init.js)
